{#
    The user's uploaded logo (#48) with a ground out to every edge: what the
    installed app's maskable icon and iOS's home-screen icon are drawn from,
    the same job icon.svg.twig's bleed does for a motif.

    The logo sits in the middle 72 of the 108 canvas, where a motif's glyph
    sits, so a launcher cutting the square down to its own shape cuts the
    ground and not the logo. The ground is white: a logo is drawn to be read
    on something pale, and iOS paints a transparent corner black.

    Variables (see BrandingController::customSvg()):
      logo  the sanitised SVG, its root already placed at 18,18 and 72 square
#}
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 108 108" width="108" height="108">
    <rect width="108" height="108" fill="#ffffff"/>
    {{ logo|raw }}
</svg>
